   "about": "compatibility",
   "version": "0.5.0",
   "text": "Please index Zotero AI Notes v0.5.0 for Zotero 9 and 10, superseding the earlier v0.4.2/v0.4.3 request.\n\nThis pre-release adds a PDF-bound reader Q&A sidebar, separate local conversations, follow-up questions, source-page citations, and user-selected Q&A collection into Zotero notes. Collected answers are labeled AI-assisted explanations.\n\nRelease: https://github.com/STRUGGLE1999/zotero-ai-notes/releases/tag/v0.5.0\nAsset: https://github.com/STRUGGLE1999/zotero-ai-notes/releases/download/v0.5.0/zotero-ai-notes-0.5.0.xpi\nCompatibility: Zotero 9.0–10.0.*\nSHA-256: 51f1932839d117d2757e6874d30102c056ce4deb704ff6f162d3ef10b618cf6d\n\nValidation: npm run check and GitHub CI passed (87 tests); macOS Zotero 10.0.6 verified PDF switching, follow-ups with citations, draft preservation and saving selected Q&A. Windows/Linux hands-on regression remains pending. Keyword retrieval uses up to six page excerpts; scanned PDFs and semantic retrieval are not supported yet.\n\nManifest: https://github.com/STRUGGLE1999/zotero-ai-notes/blob/main/addon/manifest.json\nAutomatic updates: https://github.com/STRUGGLE1999/zotero-ai-notes/blob/main/updates.json",
   "url": "https://github.com/iliasbeshimov/zoteroplugins.org/issues/2",
   "status": "fixed",
   "reply": "You published 0.5.0 as a full release on 4 November, and the card now describes it: it works with Zotero 9 and 10, and every check of its code came out low. Thanks for moving it over.\n\nYour case also showed a gap on our side: a plugin whose own update address serves a newer version than its latest full release. We're deciding how cards should handle that for every plugin at once.",
   "repliedAt": "2026-11-05"
  }
